From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: kierandrewett <kieran@drewett.dev>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 03:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] backend: refresh cursors when stream inhibition changes

Adding an embedded area or monitor stream previously changed only the
inhibitor list. A stationary hardware cursor retained an empty software
overlay, so FORCE_CURSORS could paint a frame without the cursor. Removing
the stream likewise left the renderer stale until another cursor update.

Use the existing update_cursors() traversal after each list mutation. It
invalidates and refreshes all active sprites, tolerates sprites without a
renderer, and lets the native renderer evaluate the remaining inhibitors.
Hidden and metadata streams do not enter this path.

Base: 138a14fbeef09d49ebf5be8a0cb83b042dd5c841 (Mutter 51.0)
---
 src/backends/meta-backend.c | 7 +++++++
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/backends/meta-backend.c b/src/backends/meta-backend.c
--- a/src/backends/meta-backend.c
+++ b/src/backends/meta-backend.c
@@ -1957,6 +1957,10 @@
 
   priv->hw_cursor_inhibitors = g_list_prepend (priv->hw_cursor_inhibitors,
                                                inhibitor);
+
+  /* Embedded streams need the software overlay before their first frame,
+   * even when no pointer motion follows the inhibition change. */
+  update_cursors (backend);
 }
 
 void
@@ -1967,6 +1971,9 @@
 
   priv->hw_cursor_inhibitors = g_list_remove (priv->hw_cursor_inhibitors,
                                               inhibitor);
+
+  /* Re-evaluate every sprite against the remaining inhibitors. */
+  update_cursors (backend);
 }
 
 void
